1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:02,660
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,597
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,197
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

4
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:10,456
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,975
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,420
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:16,620
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:19,060
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,237
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,517
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,160
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:40,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

14
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:52,577
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,137
That legendary place.

18
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,897
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:06,657
Is only legendary.

20
00:01:06,740 --> 00:01:10,117
Until someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,557
Through it all.

22
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,497
Through all the trouble and times.

23
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:16,817
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

24
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:21,380
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,240
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,217
So come aboard and bring along.

27
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,560
All your hopes and dreams.

28
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,877
Together we will find everything.

29
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,040
That we're looking for.

30
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:39,677
There's always room for you.

31
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:42,420
If you want to be my friend.

32
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,800
We are, we are on a cruise.

33
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,720
We are.

34
00:01:56,440 --> 00:01:58,720
Now, which one of you is Arlong?

35
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:01,220
Well, that just happens to be my name.

36
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:03,080
You can call me Luffy.

37
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:07,660
Luffy, what are you
supposed to be? A pirate.

38
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:09,880
Hold it right there.

39
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,942
Where do you think you're going?

40
00:02:13,540 --> 00:02:15,300
You want to talk to the boss?

41
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:17,891
Well, you got to talk to us first, get it?

42
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,160
So let's talk.

43
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,419
That's far enough.

44
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:23,570
Move it!

45
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:29,140
So, what does a pirate want with me?

46
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,560
Who the hell are you?

47
00:03:00,480 --> 00:03:01,920
Luffy, help me.

48
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,840
That's making our navigator cry!

49
00:03:10,140 --> 00:03:12,500
Back off, you're out of your league.

50
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,660
Jeez, you just had to
run on ahead by yourself.

51
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,597
Don't worry, I can handle
these bozos on my own.

52
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,120
Aw, you fool.

53
00:03:24,360 --> 00:03:26,831
I never said anything about being worried.

54
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:30,120
I just don't want you
hogging all the action. Oh.

55
00:03:31,320 --> 00:03:36,020
Well, I just want to let you guys know
that I don't mind if you hog at all.

56
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,760
I see you're raring to go, as usual.

57
00:03:40,660 --> 00:03:41,490
It's him!

58
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:44,417
That's the unknown swordsman
I was telling you about!

59
00:03:44,500 --> 00:03:46,920
Roa Noah Zoro. I thought so.

60
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,640
That bastard tricked me.

61
00:03:48,820 --> 00:03:50,057
I can't believe it.

62
00:03:50,140 --> 00:03:50,980
I fell for it.

63
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:52,374
Look, Sian and Yanker.

64
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,640
Wait, hook, lion, and sinker.

65
00:03:55,920 --> 00:03:57,360
Hey, look, long nose.

66
00:03:58,300 --> 00:03:59,880
But he's dead!

67
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,780
We saw Nami kill him!

68
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:04,740
But Nami was a traitor all along.

69
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,660
Just as I suspected.

70
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,680
Who are those guys?

71
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:19,430
Hold it!

72
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,957
That guy just decked Arlong.

73
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:24,900
Unbelievable!

74
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:29,497
No human should be able to do that.

75
00:04:29,580 --> 00:04:30,760
Are they?

76
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:33,300
Didn't we tell you?

77
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:36,477
Just stay back here Now do you understand

78
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:38,557
why we're keeping you
away from that fight?

79
00:04:38,640 --> 00:04:41,600
You guys will just get
in their way But why?

80
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:46,649
That's what I don't understand What
reason could they possibly have to fight?

81
00:04:47,380 --> 00:04:48,210
Reason?

82
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,820
Big Sis Nami was crying

83
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:59,680
Do they need any more reason than
that to put their lives on the line?

84
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,780
A pirate, of course.

85
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:09,260
This is all starting to make sense now!

86
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:13,560
You've been after Nami
this whole time. But.

87
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:18,760
The girl is mine and
I'm not giving her up!

88
00:05:19,980 --> 00:05:23,260
A bunch of idiots like you
aren't worth Arlong's time!

89
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:26,080
We know how to deal with you!

90
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,520
Not that.

91
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:37,620
Oh, no, it's here!

92
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,680
What is going on here, guys?

93
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:45,880
Mama, rise!

94
00:05:53,080 --> 00:05:54,460
It's a monster!

95
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:59,059
That's the beast from the Grand Line
that destroyed the town of Gosa!

96
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,600
It's actually real! Oh no!

97
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,240
It's Momo!

98
00:06:22,520 --> 00:06:23,980
Well, look who's back.

99
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:26,199
Seems he's a friend of the fishmen.

100
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:30,720
Hey, stop!

101
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:32,420
Where are you going?

102
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,260
Get back here, Mama!

103
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:36,540
You can't just leave! Mama!

104
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:38,530
Leaving?

105
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:41,020
Now, now, isn't that a shame?

106
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:50,220
But, I suppose if you really want to
run away, Then who am I to stop you?

107
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,040
Well then...

108
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,960
It's coming right before us!

109
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:11,680
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

110
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:12,730
I'm sorry!

111
00:07:16,800 --> 00:07:19,240
You're all mine, you dumb cow.

112
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:31,660
Looks like he's got a
plan for once. We'll see.

113
00:07:31,880 --> 00:07:33,880
I've got a bad feeling about this.

114
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:53,700
His arm's drenched!

115
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:59,180
So he must have devil
fruit powers. Powers?

116
00:07:59,460 --> 00:08:00,420
Aw, who cares?

117
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:01,370
Attack!

118
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,337
Hey, let's get out of here.

119
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:05,250
Whoa, wait.

120
00:08:05,333 --> 00:08:06,217
What's he gonna do?

121
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,359
I'm not sure if I want to find out.

122
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:10,420
Time for something new!

123
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,620
Gum-Gum!

124
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,640
IT WILL!

125
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:31,828
Alright, that's it, Arlong!

126
00:08:31,940 --> 00:08:33,337
I'm done playing games with you!

127
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:35,697
I didn't come here to beat
down all your cronies!

128
00:08:35,780 --> 00:08:38,020
I came here to teach you a lesson!

129
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:40,097
So step up!

130
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:42,740
Oh, I will. Don't worry.

131
00:08:44,380 --> 00:08:48,439
Actually, I was just thinking about
how painfully I'll end your life.

132
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:50,860
That was the worst plan ever!

133
00:08:51,140 --> 00:08:54,022
Yeah, well, you're trying
to kill all of us, too!

134
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,460
That boy's incredible.

135
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:05,218
I just can't believe there's a human
who can throw that giant monster!

136
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:08,540
It's as if the gods
themselves are fighting.

137
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,597
How dare you hurt our brother?

138
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:18,997
Very well, it seems that we
must now join in the fight!

139
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:22,577
Now you'll get an education in
the inferiority of your species!

140
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:26,380
Oh really, I'd like to see that!

141
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:30,897
Relax, sir!

142
00:09:30,980 --> 00:09:32,317
Let us handle this!

143
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:36,097
If you go on one of your
rampages to squash these insects,

144
00:09:36,180 --> 00:09:39,060
you destroy all of Arlong Park. Choo!

145
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:45,240
Please, just let us kill these weaklings!

146
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:47,200
All right, they're yours.

147
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:54,360
Uh, guys, there's something
I should tell you.

148
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:56,760
What the hell's that octopus doing?

149
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:00,186
Octopus is best when
it's cut thin and salted.

150
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:04,217
Add some olive oil and paprika and it
makes the perfect snack while drinking.

151
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:07,120
So listen to me, guys,
I'm kind of in trouble.

152
00:10:07,420 --> 00:10:08,260
Take this!

153
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,300
Zero vision!

154
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:11,280
Hachi Inchie!

155
00:10:16,700 --> 00:10:17,530
Idiot!

156
00:10:17,613 --> 00:10:19,204
How come you didn't dodge that?

157
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,740
I can't see Squat!

158
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,440
Now to finish you off!

159
00:10:28,380 --> 00:10:30,615
Come on, get out of there, Loopy, run!

160
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,297
Yeah, that's the problem.

161
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,920
I can't run.

162
00:10:35,140 --> 00:10:36,360
I can't even walk.

163
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,840
My feet are kind of stuck.

164
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:46,077
But you're the one who stuck them
into the ground in the first place!

165
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,454
Always thinking ahead.

166
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:52,440
One Hachi inkjet served on the rocks!

167
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:11,520
You're such a pain.

168
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:14,760
Sanji, that was so
totally awesomely awesome!

169
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:19,200
Looks like I ended up picking one
hell of an idiot to be my captain.

170
00:11:19,660 --> 00:11:20,840
We all did.

171
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,480
Luffy's great! Hey!

172
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:26,597
But the truth is that our idiot captain is

173
00:11:26,680 --> 00:11:29,300
far better than a gang
who'd prey on a lady.

174
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,220
A lady, huh?

175
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:33,650
Huh?

176
00:11:33,733 --> 00:11:36,100
You rushed into certain
death for one lousy girl?

177
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,840
Lousy girl?

178
00:11:38,320 --> 00:11:40,540
If you insult Nami one more time,

179
00:11:40,680 --> 00:11:44,037
I can promise that you'll go
from fish man to fish sticks.

180
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:45,000
Got that?

181
00:11:45,340 --> 00:11:48,200
Your skills are quite
exceptional for a human,

182
00:11:48,520 --> 00:11:52,638
but I must admit that chivalry from
a pirate seems just a little fake.

183
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,577
I'm damn good at what I do.

184
00:11:56,660 --> 00:11:58,757
And I guarantee you there's nothing fake.

185
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,820
About my desire to help
a beautiful lady in need.

186
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:06,517
Looks like I'll be acquainting you.

187
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,600
With the true superiority
of the fishman's species.

188
00:12:12,820 --> 00:12:15,880
Nice work, but they're still stuck. Still?

189
00:12:16,180 --> 00:12:17,356
They're still stuck?

190
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:23,900
We could pull all day And I bet my
legs would still be stuck in there.

191
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,517
Hey, are you trying at all?

192
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,557
Or do you want to stay stuck here?

193
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:33,660
Maybe no one told you that the penalty for
playing around in Arlong Park was just...

194
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:37,337
Come on, get unstuck already, get unstuck!

195
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:38,773
Please, Luffy, come on!

196
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,070
Come here!

197
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:42,500
Hey, Octopus.

198
00:12:43,160 --> 00:12:45,513
They're a little bit busy at the moment.

199
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:47,840
Why don't you take me on?

200
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,920
Oooh, you're Zoro!

201
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:52,220
I forgot!

202
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:54,698
You can't get away with tricking me!

203
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:03,240
And how dare you mercilessly
slaughter so many of my brothers!

204
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:05,920
That stuff's old news, Octopus Man.

205
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:09,277
I personally don't care what reasons
you have for wanting to kill me.

206
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,889
The situation has changed.

207
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:13,420
You see, the tables have turned.

208
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:16,297
You're not the hunters
anymore, understand?

209
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:19,057
Now it's you fish freaks
who are being hunted

210
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:22,600
tell him Zoro that octopus guy is yours

211
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:36,357
Hey, I'm back.

212
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:41,920
Oh You're dead I get it now.

213
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:44,560
You must actually want me to kill you

214
00:13:49,420 --> 00:13:50,320
Hold on.

215
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:53,580
Wasn't that the guy who
saved Genzo's life earlier?

216
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,430
Hey, wait.

217
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:58,561
You're the people from Cocoyashi.

218
00:13:58,860 --> 00:14:01,057
Judging from the fact
that you all have weapons,

219
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:03,669
I can only assume that
this is a rebellion.

220
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:05,697
Then you'll all have to...

221
00:14:05,780 --> 00:14:06,721
Exploding stars!

222
00:14:07,780 --> 00:14:09,220
Get through Usa!

223
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,460
Did you think it would be easy?

224
00:14:13,820 --> 00:14:15,640
You're dealing with me now!

225
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,470
Enough!

226
00:14:18,553 --> 00:14:20,775
I'm going to get rid of you right now.

227
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,140
Who is that lad?

228
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:28,300
Brave one minute and cowardly the next.

229
00:14:28,440 --> 00:14:29,740
He's a baffling man.

230
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:34,460
Get back here, Long Nose!

231
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:36,600
Oh, you're one to talk, Big Mouth!

232
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,960
Why are these people pirates?

233
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:47,037
You morons are a pathetic sight to behold.

234
00:14:47,120 --> 00:14:48,757
I'm sick of watching this now.

235
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,977
Get out of my way!

236
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:52,997
But sir, there's no
reason to go on a rampage.

237
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,217
Think of our long park.

238
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,897
Don't worry. I won't.

239
00:14:55,980 --> 00:14:58,417
I just thought of a fun game that's all.

240
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,940
Now you're going down!

241
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:09,777
Do you honestly think your sad
little group can defeat us?

242
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,660
So what if we do?

243
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,180
Yeah, so what if we do, huh?

244
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:15,640
Now let go!

245
00:15:15,940 --> 00:15:17,764
You got something to say to us?

246
00:15:28,580 --> 00:15:31,997
Did you know that those with
Devil Fruit powers can't swim?

247
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:36,337
But honestly, anybody in this situation
would sink right to the bottom!

248
00:15:36,420 --> 00:15:39,600
Gum-Gum Pistol! The sea! No!

249
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:43,140
Gum-Gum Pistol!

250
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:48,140
OUCHI!

251
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:50,500
You fool!

252
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,250
How pointless.

253
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,320
Luffy!

254
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,540
Damn you!

255
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:18,837
Wait don't be stupid those fishmen can't
wait for us to jump in the water after him.

256
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:22,214
They'd have an obvious advantage
in an underwater fight.

257
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:27,597
There's only one way to
save Luffy we've got to

258
00:16:27,680 --> 00:16:30,117
take these guys out at
the same time then go in.

259
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:33,797
Water there's no time come on let's do it.

260
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:38,237
Yeah so how long can he
hold out time? Is ticking.

261
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,657
Oh so that's the game

262
00:16:40,740 --> 00:16:45,997
I get it you can take

263
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:49,440
the fish you slice and trim the octopus.

264
00:17:02,820 --> 00:17:04,080
This is bad.

265
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,940
I'm almost out of breath.

266
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:07,740
What now?

267
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:09,117
He can't help himself.

268
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,030
What do we do?

269
00:17:10,240 --> 00:17:11,880
Big Bro Luffy's gonna die!

270
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:22,400
They can't even breathe underwater.

271
00:17:22,920 --> 00:17:25,740
Humans are such pitiful
creatures, aren't they?

272
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,640
Hey, calamari, let's go.

273
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:36,520
Game, game!

274
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:39,640
I'll kick your ass in five seconds flat.

275
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,617
We don't have more than three.

276
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,120
Hey, what's the rush?

277
00:17:43,760 --> 00:17:46,113
You're both running headlong into death.

278
00:17:46,420 --> 00:17:48,773
None of you will leave this place alone.

279
00:18:01,020 --> 00:18:02,460
Oh, crap!

280
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:04,420
I'm gonna be killed!

281
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:09,780
I'll beat his ass real quick
and then come save you, Luffy.

282
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,800
A-chi-ing-cha!

283
00:18:19,180 --> 00:18:21,940
No, you bastard! My hair!

284
00:18:24,780 --> 00:18:25,960
But it's okay.

285
00:18:26,220 --> 00:18:27,120
It's only hair.

286
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,960
It'll grow back. Huh?

287
00:18:29,220 --> 00:18:31,380
Now, Zoro, you can't beat me.

288
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:37,480
I have six hands that will mesmerize
you with their wiggly beauty. Shut up!

289
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:38,570
Oh, jeez!

290
00:18:38,653 --> 00:18:40,340
Triple! Sword! Catch!

291
00:18:40,700 --> 00:18:43,960
Now, you will see my skills!

292
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,500
That hurt!

293
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,800
I don't have time for this crap.

294
00:18:51,940 --> 00:18:52,770
No, not now.

295
00:18:53,580 --> 00:18:55,120
Is he still hurt?

296
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:57,517
Lose focus and you lose your luck!

297
00:18:57,600 --> 00:19:00,160
I bet you taste good! Butter!

298
00:19:00,620 --> 00:19:03,500
I've got no time left! No time!

299
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:07,940
Why don't you die?!

300
00:19:10,940 --> 00:19:11,770
Too bad!

301
00:19:11,853 --> 00:19:13,820
Hunchy suckers are stuck!

302
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,300
Don't just stick there!

303
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,852
Get down here and fight!

304
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:21,490
Damn coward.

305
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,002
Stupid octopus.

306
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,237
He's just trying to waste our time.

307
00:19:26,320 --> 00:19:27,997
But if we try to save Luffy now,

308
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,717
they'll just drag us to the
bottom of the sea and we'll drown.

309
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:34,037
If we sit here and do nothing,
then Luffy drowns for sure.

310
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:36,117
We've got to think of a way to help him.

311
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:37,280
Yeah. Hold on.

312
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:42,497
What good are the two of you going to do
in the sea when you both can barely walk?

313
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:45,477
If you're trying to figure out
a way to save that young man,

314
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:49,400
Then I believe I should be the
one to volunteer ahead of you!

315
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:51,021
You'll save him?

316
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:53,417
Genzo, I'm coming with you.

317
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,057
Let's do it! I'm in.

318
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:56,317
I'm going alone.

319
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:58,517
The fishmen will suspect that we're up to

320
00:19:58,600 --> 00:20:00,617
something if we go with
such a large crowd.

321
00:20:00,700 --> 00:20:03,517
And I fear doing so may
cause more harm than good.

322
00:20:03,600 --> 00:20:04,757
But we could help them.

323
00:20:04,840 --> 00:20:05,817
Now another word about it.

324
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:08,557
There's no point endangering
more people than we have to.

325
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,400
I must go alone.

326
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:12,840
Yes, thank you.

327
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:14,654
We're counting on you.

328
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:16,960
But please, hurry.

329
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:18,260
Hold on.

330
00:20:19,180 --> 00:20:20,840
Genzo, I'm going too.

331
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:22,820
No, Gecko, you're hurt.

332
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:24,837
You're not going to
leave me out of this when

333
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:27,137
those guys are fighting
for my sister's life.

334
00:20:27,220 --> 00:20:28,120
You can't.

335
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,310
Fine.

336
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:32,820
Come on, we have to hurry. Right.

337
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:35,860
I'm sorry.

338
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:38,100
If only I was stronger.

339
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:40,340
Please save Luffy.

340
00:20:40,760 --> 00:20:41,819
Don't be too late.

341
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:49,937
Hey, I have a question that I've
been meaning to ask you, Zoro.

342
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:54,077
You're famous for your three-sword
technique, so why are you only using one?

343
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,377
You're running scared with one.

344
00:20:55,460 --> 00:20:56,577
Why would I need three?

345
00:20:56,660 --> 00:20:57,490
Shut up!

346
00:20:57,573 --> 00:20:59,417
I've just been playing around with you.

347
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:01,620
Actually, humans can't defeat me.

348
00:21:01,820 --> 00:21:04,497
I can tell you why, but I think
it'd be more fun to show you.

349
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,160
Yeah, show. I like that.

350
00:21:06,380 --> 00:21:09,380
I think you're really going
to enjoy it a lot, too.

351
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:10,990
Damn it.

352
00:21:11,073 --> 00:21:12,980
I can't fight back the pain.

353
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,920
Crap, I thought as much.

354
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:27,077
You still haven't recovered
from your fight with Hawkeye?

355
00:21:27,160 --> 00:21:27,990
Zoro!

356
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:35,720
Now you may tremble in fear
at Hachi's way of six blades.

357
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:39,197
Hey, you're not supposed to die yet!

358
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:40,809
I haven't even killed you.

359
00:21:43,480 --> 00:21:45,597
No! Zoro! I knew it!

360
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:46,837
He's been faking it!

361
00:21:46,920 --> 00:21:47,860
So true.

362
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:52,937
The way he's been pummeled would kill any
normal guy, but he tries to fight anyway.

363
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:53,902
What'd you say?

364
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:57,737
I thought it was strange.

365
00:21:57,820 --> 00:22:02,257
He walked around just like nothing had
happened after such a horrible fight.

366
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:03,700
He's laid out flat.

367
00:22:10,860 --> 00:22:13,820
I told you to pay attention
to me, you weakling.

368
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:16,720
I'm a 40th Don in Fishman Karate.

369
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:18,477
Whoa, what the...

370
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:20,300
What the hell just happened?

371
00:22:21,420 --> 00:22:22,250
Sanji?

372
00:22:22,333 --> 00:22:23,660
It can't be him!

373
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:27,430
Sanji!

374
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:32,120
They're taking care of, Arlong.

375
00:22:32,460 --> 00:22:34,557
What would you like us to do with Zoro?

376
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:35,875
What a waste of time.

377
00:22:36,220 --> 00:22:37,691
Just toss him in the sea.

378
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:39,196
Hardly entertaining.

379
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:43,640
Aww, that's all?

380
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:47,120
Well, they did manage
to make a bit of a mess.

381
00:22:47,380 --> 00:22:48,340
No big deal.

382
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:51,760
As long as Arlong Park
is still standing. True.

383
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:56,000
No fair!

384
00:22:56,340 --> 00:22:57,399
He killed himself!

385
00:22:57,660 --> 00:23:01,057
I never got the chance to show
him how great of a swordsman I am!

386
00:23:01,140 --> 00:23:04,857
If he could have died on one of my six
blades, I could have stolen his fame!

387
00:23:04,940 --> 00:23:06,260
Well, it's no matter.

388
00:23:06,480 --> 00:23:09,497
There isn't a human alive that can
compare to my way of six blades!

389
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:14,051
Behold the superior power that only a
six-armed Master Swordsman can attain!

390
00:23:22,800 --> 00:23:23,960
Enough, Hachi.

391
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:28,637
I understand how you must feel, but if
you continue this little demonstration?

392
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,180
you'll destroy Arlong Park. Oh!

393
00:23:32,260 --> 00:23:33,560
I'm sorry.

394
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:37,380
I forgot I could destroy stuff.

395
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:38,737
Don't get carried away.

396
00:23:38,820 --> 00:23:40,137
I'm fine now.

397
00:23:40,220 --> 00:23:43,117
Way of six blades.

398
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:44,580
What a loser!

399
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:51,960
Way to go!

400
00:23:54,040 --> 00:23:55,580
You're not dead.

401
00:23:56,340 --> 00:23:58,297
Let me make this clear for you.

402
00:23:58,380 --> 00:24:00,720
You're sorry excuse for a swordsman

403
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:02,680
There's a certain man.

404
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:06,180
I have to face and then till I see him

405
00:24:07,300 --> 00:24:10,520
Death himself cannot touch me.

406
00:24:27,040 --> 00:24:27,917
Ah!

407
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,760
He's still alive!

408
00:24:30,160 --> 00:24:31,440
All right, big bro!

409
00:24:32,820 --> 00:24:35,700
That's the best punch that fish man's got.

410
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:41,257
The old man's kicks were a
hundred times worse than that!

411
00:24:41,340 --> 00:24:43,040
And I never even died.

412
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:45,700
Stop following me!

413
00:25:01,440 --> 00:25:05,017
I'm alone, but always now
I'm done, I'll keep you near.

414
00:25:05,100 --> 00:25:09,720
As I drift away, I pray you'll
watch me as I disappear.

415
00:25:15,580 --> 00:25:19,677
As I watch the sunrise, I begin to wonder?

416
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:24,357
What could be the reason
it's so hot inside?

417
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:30,477
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

418
00:25:30,560 --> 00:25:33,220
It's because of you.

419
00:25:35,940 --> 00:25:38,557
Show me how to catch those feelings.

420
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,657
Get them to come back to me.

421
00:25:40,740 --> 00:25:42,957
I'll do what I must be.

422
00:25:43,040 --> 00:25:45,717
Because they're everything I want to be.

423
00:25:45,800 --> 00:25:48,237
Wrap these arms around my dreams.

424
00:25:48,320 --> 00:25:50,317
And pull them back from yesterday.

425
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:55,720
If I'm holding hands with you,
I'm sure that we can make the way.
